This software implements Australian tax, superannuation, social-security and aged-care rules from
publicly available government and legislative sources cited per parameter in /parameters and
/verification. It is not financial product advice, is not endorsed by the Australian Taxation
Office, ASIC, Services Australia, the Department of Social Services, the Department of Health,
Disability and Ageing, or any Commonwealth agency, and is provided under the Apache License 2.0
WITHOUT WARRANTY. Users who provide financial advice remain responsible for validating outputs and
for compliance with the Corporations Act 2001 and their AFS licence conditions.

Government material: ATO material is used under the ATO's copyright notice, which permits reuse
provided no endorsement is implied. Values are stored as short structured data with attribution;
no long passages of government text are reproduced.

Parameter currency statement: each release embeds a parameter release hash and currency date
(src/generated/parameters.json, docs/PARAMETERS.md) identifying the latest source incorporated.

Third-party runtime dependencies: decimal.js (MIT), zod (MIT). The web interface bundles React
(MIT). Development tools are not distributed; a licence scan of node_modules (2026-10-11) found
MIT, Apache-2.0, ISC, BSD-3-Clause and MPL-2.0 (lightningcss, build-time CSS tooling only) and no
GPL/AGPL packages.
